Message-ID: <199610112314.RAA00346@ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca>
Date: Fri, 11 Oct 1996 17:14:08 -0600 (MDT)
From: Michal Jaegermann <michal@ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca>
Subject: Re: UDB, RH4: Slow/Hang  Boot
In-Reply-To: <1.5.4.32.19961011210149.0069aaa8@execpc.com>

> 
> I have a similar problem, but I still have RH 3.0.3.  The problem did not
> occur with the original kernel shipped with 3.0.3.  The problem only started
> after I upgraded the kernel.  

I bet that you have a wrong rooting table on a loopback (net address
of 127.0.0.1 instead of 127.0.0.0).  This is a bug in Red Hat
distribution and is not limited to Alpha.  Older kernels could live
with it, but newer ones are unhappy and rightly so.

In ifup-lo you should have a line which reads
route add -net 127.0.0.0
and not
'route add -net 127.0.0.1'  or 'route add -net ${IPADDR}' or something
like that.

  Michal

