This is a sure sign of 64-bit uncleanliness in top.

Notice the pc is 0x20004f90 when the normal program text lies
above 0x120000000.  Someone has cast a function pointer to an
integer and expected it to be useful afterwards.

Incidentally, under normal conditions the entire low 4GB of
the address space is unused just to catch these sorts of errors.

