From: Jim Nance <jlnance@avanticorp.com>
Subject: Re: OK I got into the SRM but.....
In-Reply-To: <199610181414.KAA12446@mail.pulse-sys.com>

> I got into the SRM and booted the RedHat floppy but the HD was mounted as
> the root dev so the Craftworks installation came up.  How do I use the SRM to
> boot the floopy not mount the hda as the root device?

At the SRM prompt you should be able to say:

d dva0 -fl i

This should bring you up to an aboot prompt, at which you would say
something like:

vmlinux root=/dev/scda ro

Jim

