From rusling@linux.reo.dec.com Mon Oct 21 10:07:43 1996
Message-ID: <199610211206.MAA00456@linux.reo.dec.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Oct 1996 12:06:22 +0000
From: David A Rusling <rusling@linux.reo.dec.com>
Subject: Re: building Milo on RH 4.0 (ELF)?

The palcode in MILO is a pre-built image which has been stripped.  The
sysgen tool adds it into the MILO image.  MILO itself is a stripped image
and requires no help from a loader.  Linload just dumps the whole thing into
memory and says "go".  Sometime this week I'll produce a diffs file which
will allow MILO to build on ELF without the ECOFF BIOS emulation code...

Dave

